From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Kane <jkane@tds.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:26:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] [VectraOS] Concurrency with VectraOS's global and main
 executors

SWIFT_CONCURRENCY_GLOBAL_EXECUTOR=vectraos: PlatformExecutorVectraOS.swift's
factory gives a default executor of one worker thread per CPU croi runs
(td_cpu_count) and a main executor the main thread runs once the async
main hands it over, over VectraOSGlobalExecutor.cpp (adapted from
swift-on-vectra's): ready jobs in priority buckets, delayed ones by
deadline on the monotonic clock, under our pthreads' mutex, with the
threads sleeping on a croi port (td_port_wait) until a wake packet or
the soonest deadline. Clock.cpp takes the POSIX clock branches; Actor.cpp
skips <sys/syscall.h>, which it doesn't use; the frontend imports
_Concurrency implicitly for *-vectraos.
---
